  "id": "Compound::DB00280 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Disopyramide, a drug known for its effects on muscarinic acetylcholine receptors, appears to interact with Chrm1 through a shared pathway involving G-protein coupled receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Disopyramide binds to Chrm2, which is involved in the regulation of G-protein coupled receptor activity. This activity is then participated by Chrm1, indicating a potential functional link between Disopyramide and Chrm1. The consistent interaction across different pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Disopyramide modulates the activity of Chrm2, which in turn influences Chrm1 through a G-protein coupled signaling cascade. The overlapping roles of Chrm2 in different receptor activities suggest that Disopyramide may exert its effects by targeting a common intermediary, Chrm2, which then engages Chrm1 via a shared signaling pathway. This integrated view underscores the role of Chrm2 as a critical mediator in the relationship between Disopyramide and Chrm1.",
